# MIDI CC in (fm1-x0x#15): a CC on a part's channel (909 10, 808 11, 303 A 2, 303 B 3, break 4) or on MIX
# MIDI CH (1) sets its pot as the knob would. CC OUT starts OFF: nothing goes out.
wait 300
expect ccoutset 0
# CC 123 (all notes off) on 303 A's channel ends the note MIDI holds there; CC 120 (all sound off) on the
# break's lets go of its slices (their sends off, so no tail is left)
param 5 2 1 0
param 5 2 2 0
param 5 4 1 0
param 5 4 2 0
midi 91 30 64
wait 300
peakreset
wait 100
expect peak_db_min -30
midi B1 7B 00
wait 1500
peakreset
wait 300
expect peak_db_max -60
midi 93 24 7F
wait 300
peakreset
wait 100
expect peak_db_min -30
midi B3 78 00
wait 1500
peakreset
wait 300
expect peak_db_max -60
# 303 A: CC 16 Cutoff, 74 its alias; a switch (Wave, CC 21) turns over at 64
midi B1 10 40
wait 30
expect sound2.0.0 64
midi B1 4A 7F
wait 30
expect sound2.0.0 127
midi B2 15 3F
wait 30
expect sound2.1.5 0
midi B2 15 40
wait 30
expect sound2.1.5 1
# 303 B: Tune is CC 24 (index 6), DrvType CC 26 (0..2)
midi B2 18 00
midi B2 1A 7F
wait 30
expect sound2.1.6 0
expect sound2.1.9 2
# the 909's voices by name: BD Level (CC 102), CH Decay (77: its Decay is pot 0), RS has no Decay (75)
midi B9 66 20
midi B9 4D 10
wait 30
expect sound0.0.3 32
expect sound0.7.0 16
expect sound0.5.0 103
midi B9 4B 05
wait 30
expect sound0.5.0 103
expect sound0.5.1 62
# the 808's CY Tune (28: its Tune is pot 2), the kit's Accent (12)
midi BA 1C 11
midi BA 0C 22
wait 30
expect sound1.8.2 17
expect sound1.11.1 34
# a part's mixer on its own channel: 909 level (7), pan (10), reverb (91), delay (93)
midi B9 07 50
midi B9 0A 00
midi B9 5B 7F
midi B9 5D 40
wait 30
expect sound5.0.0 80
expect sound5.0.3 0
expect sound5.0.1 127
expect sound5.0.2 64
# MIX MIDI CH (1): the parts' levels 102-106, the master's FILTER (19, 74) and RESO (71), TAPE (25)
midi B0 68 30
wait 30
expect sound5.2.0 48
midi B0 13 20
wait 30
expect sound6.0.13 32
midi B0 4A 60
midi B0 47 7F
midi B0 19 7F
wait 30
expect sound6.0.13 96
expect sound6.0.10 127
expect sound4.1.0 127
expect sound4.0.13 1
# the master's COMP (17), the delay's TIME (22: 0..12)
midi B0 11 7F
midi B0 16 7F
wait 30
expect sound6.0.12 127
expect sound4.0.8 12
# the break: Filter (16), Level (17), Pitch (18: 0..24)
midi B3 10 00
midi B3 11 40
midi B3 12 7F
wait 30
expect sound3.0.2 0
expect sound3.0.0 64
expect sound3.0.1 24
# a CC on a channel nobody has does nothing; a part's CC on another part's channel neither
midi B4 10 00
midi B9 10 00
wait 30
expect sound2.0.0 127
# nothing went out: CC OUT is OFF
expect ccouts 0
# undo takes a sweep as one step: a run of CCs, then one undo puts the cutoff back where it began
wait 600
midi B1 10 10
wait 20
midi B1 10 20
wait 20
midi B1 10 30
wait 600
expect sound2.0.0 48
press HOME
tap REC
release HOME
expect sound2.0.0 127
# recording, playing: a CC writes its lane, as a knob does
expect lanes 0
tap REC
tap PLAY
wait 200
midi B1 11 10
wait 150
midi B1 11 30
wait 150
midi B1 11 50
wait 300
expect lanes 1
tap PLAY
tap REC
wait 200
# a screen reader says nothing for CCs, even for a knob on the page showing (the 909 BD's TUNE lights)
listen
wait 600
said 909
midi B9 14 30
wait 50
expect sound0.0.0 48
midi B1 10 20
wait 600
said_none
# a knob turned by hand after them is said
turn K1 1
wait 600
said TUNE 49
